+// computes them: a block is 32 consecutive columns, which one warp holds in registers, reduced with the same
+// 32-lane butterflies. So the bits are those of the norm followed by the quantization, in one launch and without
+// reading the row again. One row per block; ncols % 32 == 0; the weight is one row of ncols values.
